kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[5]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  modify_requirement,tui61,"markdown-scope-full-graded-headings","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render at minimum: graded headings (H1 bold+underlined, H2 bold, H3 bold+italic, H4-H6 italic, each with a leading hash-repeat prefix matching its level), bold/code inline, fenced code blocks (with syntect highlighting, no background/border/language-label), unordered lists (bullet marker), ordered lists (auto-incrementing number marker colored light_blue), task lists, blockquotes (with a visible greater-than prefix on every physical row), tables (aligned columns, no border lines), and CJK-aware paragraph wrapping. Syntax highlighting of fenced code blocks is provided by a syntect backend (tui70/tui71); OSC8 hyperlinks and streaming incremental markdown parsing remain excluded. Streaming text in the mutable last line stays plain text; markdown rendering applies only after a line is finalized and committed to scrollback.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui66,"blockquote-visual-prefix-gt","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render blockquote lines with a visible leading prefix of the greater-than character followed by a space colored with the quote style, so blockquotes are distinguishable from plain paragraph text on terminals where the dim color difference is hard to perceive. The prefix MUST appear on every physical row of the blockquote (including wrapped continuation rows), and MUST indent for nested blockquotes (each nesting level adds another greater-than, so a double-nested quote renders with a doubled prefix). Evidence: codex uses a vertical-bar left border for blockquotes; pi keeps the greater-than prefix; the c355 blockquote renderer applied only dim style with no glyph, which was visually indistinguishable from normal text.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui71,"code-highlight-theme-adaptive","The TUI code block syntax highlighting (via syntect + two-face, default-fancy pure-Rust backend) MUST highlight fenced code blocks in recognized languages using a theme adapted to the terminal background lightness, and MUST fall back to plain unstyled text when the language is unrecognized OR the input exceeds safety limits (512 KB / 10000 lines), so rendering never blocks or panics on pathological input. Theme selection MUST pick a light theme (CatppuccinLatte) when the COLORFGBS environment variable indicates a light background (background code >= 7), and a dark theme (CatppuccinMocha) otherwise (including when COLORFGBS is unset). The selected theme MUST be cached for the process lifetime.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui78,"heading-graded-by-level","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render headings with level-graded styling: H1 MUST be bold plus underlined, H2 MUST be bold, H3 MUST be bold plus italic, and H4/H5/H6 MUST be italic. Each heading MUST carry a leading prefix of N hash characters followed by a space matching its level (so a level-1 heading renders with a single hash prefix, level-2 with a double hash prefix, etc). Evidence: codex MarkdownStyles assigns distinct styles per level and start_heading prepends the hash prefix (codex-rs/tui/src/markdown_render.rs:89-105 and 579-580); the c395 renderer applied a single bold style to all levels and dropped the prefix, flattening the document outline.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui79,"ordered-list-number-marker","The TUI MarkdownRenderer MUST render ordered list items with an auto-incrementing number marker (e.g. 1. 2. 3.) colored light_blue, incrementing from the list start value across sibling items. Unordered list items MUST render with a bullet marker. Evidence: codex start_item emits an index-followed-by-dot marker in ordered_list_marker style (codex-rs/tui/src/markdown_render.rs:772-799); the c395 renderer dropped the ordered-list start tag into a catch-all no-op, losing the number marker entirely.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[8]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui61,"graded-heading-prefix-visible","an assistant reply containing headings of multiple levels is finalized and rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,"each heading row carries a hash prefix matching its level (single hash for H1, double hash for H2, etc)"
  tui66,"blockquote-has-gt-prefix","an assistant reply containing a blockquote is finalized and rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,"each row of the blockquote carries a leading greater-than-space prefix colored with the quote style, present on wrapped continuation rows too"
  tui66,"nested-blockquote-gt-indents","a nested blockquote is rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,"the inner blockquote rows carry an additional greater-than so nesting is visually expressed as a doubled prefix"
  tui71,"light-theme-when-colorfgbs-light","the COLORFGBS environment variable is set to a value indicating a light background (e.g. 0;15) and a fenced rs code block is rendered","the highlight theme is selected and the buffer cell styles are inspected","code spans use the light theme (CatppuccinLatte) palette distinct from the dark default"
  tui71,"dark-theme-when-colorfgbs-unset","the COLORFGBS environment variable is unset and a fenced rs code block is rendered","the highlight theme is selected","code spans use the dark theme (CatppuccinMocha) matching the prior fixed behavior"
  tui78,"h1-bold-underlined","a level-1 heading is rendered via TestBackend",the heading row cell styles are inspected,"the style carries both BOLD and UNDERLINED modifiers"
  tui78,"h3-bold-italic","a level-3 heading is rendered via TestBackend",the heading row cell styles are inspected,"the style carries both BOLD and ITALIC modifiers"
  tui79,"ordered-list-numbers-increment","an assistant reply containing an ordered list (1. a / 2. b / 3. c) is finalized and rendered via TestBackend",the buffer is inspected,"the first item row carries a 1. marker, the second a 2. marker, the third a 3. marker, each colored light_blue"
